{"id": "EUVD-2026-103321", "enisaUuid": "df49d827-477b-3260-9b76-a63ac2c771dd", "description": "phpMyFAQ 4.2.0-alpha before 4.2.0-beta contains an authentication bypass vulnerability that allows Keycloak users to take over local accounts by matching preferred_username or email. Attackers controlling a Keycloak identity with a colliding username or unverified email can log in through /auth/keycloak/authorize to bind their subject and gain superadmin privileges.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T11:21:21", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/security/advisories/GHSA-rg4w-2j3r-2hhp", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpmyfaq-4.2.0-alpha-before-4.2.0-beta-account-takeover-via-keycloak-implicit-account-linking"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111898", "GHSA-8rmr-jc2p-xv7g"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.34, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "b2d25441-a436-3392-9106-d76df3ddcc8e", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0-alpha <4.2.0-beta"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b84d5a95-537b-3682-9ebf-ccd23aa8dbf6", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}], "isExploited": false}